# Routing & Auth

## Router

React Router v6 in `App.tsx`. Layout wraps protected routes.

```
/login              PublicRoute → Login
/                   ProtectedRoute → Layout → Dashboard
/users              UsersPage
/reports            Reports
/settings/*         Settings nested routes
```

## Guards

- `ProtectedRoute`: redirects to `/login` if no `auth_token` cookie
- `PublicRoute`: redirects to `/` if token exists

## Token lifecycle

1. Login → `POST /login` (base includes `/admin`) → store token in `auth_token` cookie
2. Axios interceptor attaches Bearer header
3. Logout → `POST /logout` → erase cookie, disconnect Echo, clear Query cache

## 401 handling

Axios interceptor clears cookie and shows toast. Consider navigating to `/login` in a future enhancement.
